Third-party code
----------------

internal/sdg is a port to Go of the opensdg C library:

    https://github.com/Sonic-Amiga/opensdg
    Copyright (C) Pavel Fedin
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3.

opensdg carries no per-file copyright or licence headers; the attribution
above is taken from that repository's LICENSE.txt and commit history.

Changes made in this port, for the purposes of section 5(a) of the licence:

  - The library was translated from C to Go and restructured around Go's
    concurrency and error handling. No opensdg source is included here.
  - The direct local (non-relayed) peer connection is not present in
    opensdg and was worked out against a real frame.
  - Only the client side needed by this program was ported; the mainloop,
    socket and logging layers have no counterpart here.

The test vectors in internal/sdg/reference_test.go were generated against
opensdg's own packet layouts so that this port could be checked byte for
byte. They record the wire format of the protocol, not opensdg's code.

The upstream author asks that opensdg not be put to commercial use. That
request is stated in the opensdg README rather than in its licence, so it is
passed on here as a request and not as a term of this licence -- adding such
a term would contradict section 7 of the GNU General Public License.


